    {
      "id": "element-409",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -8505.946823367285,
      "y": 6518.051595403418,
      "width": 1290,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#645b73",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1.7,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1.2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1185817516,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 206893740,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 0,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Total = database + data + processing. A/B use a dedicated 2 vCPU / 8 GB database (~US$ 134, double with HA). C uses a small instance (~US$ 15).\nData: ~200 B per Postgres row, ~20 B per Parquet row, ~30 items per subscription. A/B use Datastream CDC at US$ 2 per GiB in the model.\nProcessing: ~US$ 5 per 100 million at 500 records/s on 1 vCPU. Excludes data lake and engineering time.\nThe model uses approximate São Paulo Cloud SQL pricing and R$ 5.55 per US dollar (reference closing rate R$ 5.56).\nUp to 100 million records, the database instance dominates the estimate.\nStudy scale: 158 million active subscriptions. A and C write about 4.7 billion records at roughly 30 items per subscription.\nA needs a larger instance. B writes 158 million rows. C at the same subscription grain is about US$ 25.",
      "originalText": "Total = database + data + processing. A/B use a dedicated 2 vCPU / 8 GB database (~US$ 134, double with HA). C uses a small instance (~US$ 15).\nData: ~200 B per Postgres row, ~20 B per Parquet row, ~30 items per subscription. A/B use Datastream CDC at US$ 2 per GiB in the model.\nProcessing: ~US$ 5 per 100 million at 500 records/s on 1 vCPU. Excludes data lake and engineering time.\nThe model uses approximate São Paulo Cloud SQL pricing and R$ 5.55 per US dollar (reference closing rate R$ 5.56).\nUp to 100 million records, the database instance dominates the estimate.\nStudy scale: 158 million active subscriptions. A and C write about 4.7 billion records at roughly 30 items per subscription.\nA needs a larger instance. B writes 158 million rows. C at the same subscription grain is about US$ 25.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "c06E",
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
