    {
      "id": "element-454",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -7085.946823367285,
      "y": 6141.051595403418,
      "width": 1120,
      "height": 356.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#26232a",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1.7,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1.2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 462601260,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 831428372,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 0,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "• Job state: prevent overlapping runs and time out orphaned running records\n• Persist the cursor in the batch transaction\n• Separate writer, purge and CDC privileges. Limit CDC to published tables\n• A/B: set max_slot_wal_keep_size and alert on replication lag\n• C: derive the object key from the batch, then create only if absent\n• Entitlements Postgres: read-only access, keyset paging and small batches without a replica\n• Registry: coordinate a replica or materialized view with the DBA. Avoid primary reads\n• Registry view exposes ID, plan, status and dates. Exclude document IDs, email and phone\n• Registry lacks a date index. Page by subscriptions.id and parallelize by ID range\n• Registry holds current state. Snapshot at month-end. Order history lives in orders\n• Incremental runs replay a recent window. Set a fixed cutoff timezone\n• Send failed subscriptions to an error table and continue the batch\n• Send a month-closed signal and per-run count to the lake\n• LGPD: define lake retention and a data-subject deletion flow\n• Rundeck: restrict triggers with ACLs, prevent concurrent runs, use Key Storage and omit PII",
      "originalText": "• Job state: prevent overlapping runs and time out orphaned running records\n• Persist the cursor in the batch transaction\n• Separate writer, purge and CDC privileges. Limit CDC to published tables\n• A/B: set max_slot_wal_keep_size and alert on replication lag\n• C: derive the object key from the batch, then create only if absent\n• Entitlements Postgres: read-only access, keyset paging and small batches without a replica\n• Registry: coordinate a replica or materialized view with the DBA. Avoid primary reads\n• Registry view exposes ID, plan, status and dates. Exclude document IDs, email and phone\n• Registry lacks a date index. Page by subscriptions.id and parallelize by ID range\n• Registry holds current state. Snapshot at month-end. Order history lives in orders\n• Incremental runs replay a recent window. Set a fixed cutoff timezone\n• Send failed subscriptions to an error table and continue the batch\n• Send a month-closed signal and per-run count to the lake\n• LGPD: define lake retention and a data-subject deletion flow\n• Rundeck: restrict triggers with ACLs, prevent concurrent runs, use Key Storage and omit PII",
